through its Law API Version 2 (https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/2/). e-Gov's terms of use (利用規約,
https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/terms) apply the Public Data License 1.0 (公共データ利用規約（第1.0版）, PDL1.0,
https://www.digital.go.jp/resources/open_data/public_data_license_v1.0) to the site's content, which allows anyone to
copy, transmit, translate and adapt it, including for commercial use, with attribution, and which the Digital Agency
states is compatible with the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0).

Attribution, as PDL1.0 asks:

    出典：e-Gov 法令検索（https://laws.e-gov.go.jp）、PDL1.0（https://www.digital.go.jp/resources/open_data/public_data_license_v1.0）
    「e-Gov 法令検索」（デジタル庁）（https://laws.e-gov.go.jp）を加工して作成（Lexifina）

("Source: e-Gov Law Search, PDL1.0. Made by Lexifina by processing e-Gov Law Search (Digital Agency).") The processing:
the consolidated text of each revision was split into one file per provision and arranged as a git history, one
commit per amending law and enforcement day; ruby readings were left out. No words were changed. This repository is
not an official publication of the Government of Japan or the Digital Agency, and the authoritative text of a law is
the one promulgated in the Official Gazette (官報).

